@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
title The unit baseline — green means no new failing test
' purpose: how a branch proves it broke nothing while the unit suite is already red on the host it is built on
' covers: mise.toml
' covers: internal/contract/mise_gates_test.go
'   the decision ............ _spec/_plans/tui-upgrades-delivery.puml (DECISIONS, D12)
'   the gate it stands in ... _spec/_plans/tui-upgrades-delivery.puml (the standing gate)
'   the full gate ........... _spec/_devops/release-gate.puml
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' ── WHY THIS EXISTS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' MEASURED 2026-11-10 at 0f34a714 (= main), darwin/arm64, with and without
' -race: `go test -count=1 ./...` fails 15 tests in 3 of 47 packages. None
' sits in a TUI package. Two fail on any host: envreg.go:153 puts
' PROVEO_GITHUB_TRANSPORT in the wrong block, and probe_test.go:30 names a
' `:latest` tag outside imagetest.Resolve. Thirteen trace to this macOS host:
' /bin/bash is 3.2, `flock` is absent, and a unix socket path under the test
' temp dir exceeds 104 bytes. The release gate runs `go test ./...` in its
' in-sandbox Linux half, where those thirteen are expected to pass.
' [Unverified] That they pass on Linux: no Linux run exists yet.
' `mise run ci` therefore exits non-zero on this host before any change, and
' a red suite cannot say whether a slice broke something.
' The Executor, 2026-11-10: "Since the failures are not TUI related, let Green
' be 'no new failing tests'".
'
' ── WHAT THE GATE DOES (2026-11-12) ───────────────────────────────────────
' `mise run baseline` is one mise run string:
'   go test [-race] -count=1 -skip='^(<[vars] unit_baseline>)$' [go_test_args]
' The list lives in mise.toml [vars] unit_baseline: one backslash-continued
' string, one name per line, joined by |. -skip drops exactly those top-level
' tests; every other failure, a build error or a panic outside a test fails
' go test, and go test's exit code is the verdict.
'   --no-race ........... drops -race, for a toolchain without cgo
'   [go_test_args]... ... packages replace ./...; go test flags pass after --
' LOST ON 2026-11-12, BY DESIGN: a listed test never runs here, so the gate
' prints no "passes here" note, and a row is a bare test name with no package
' scope (-skip is unscoped). A stale row stays silent until someone reads
' test-go, which runs every test. TestUnitBaselineRowsNameRealTests keeps each
' row a top-level test defined in exactly one tracked _test.go, so a row
' cannot skip a second test of the same name.
' HISTORY, 2026-11-10 to 2026-11-12: the gate was a Go program over
' `go test -race -count=1 -json ./...`. It listed a failing top-level test as
' "package Test", a test-less package failure as "package (package)", and
' diffed them against a unit-baseline.txt: a failure outside the list exited
' 1, a listed test that passed printed a note and exited 0, so a row could
' pass on one host type without turning the gate red on the other.
' A RED TEST GUARDS NOTHING. TestVarsSortByScopeThenName covers envreg.go.
' A slice that edits that file fixes line 153 first and drops the row.
' THE GATE DOES NOT RETRY, SO ONE KNOWN FLAKE IS LISTED. MEASURED 2026-11-10:
' TestAdbMirrorStartsWithTheSocketAddress failed in 2 of 8 full runs and passed
' 6 of 6 alone. At main it passed 3 of 3 full runs. Its helper starts a stub in
' the background, sleeps a fixed 50ms and then reads the stub's log
' (internal/contract/host_adb_lib_test.go:42-44); under a loaded full run the
' stub has not written yet. The branch adds tests and so adds load; it does
' not touch that code. The row is the 16th in the list, and the first that is
' a flake rather than a failure. A retry inside the gate would also hide a
' test that fails only in the full run's order, so the gate has none.
' [Inference] The fixed sleep is the cause; the timing was read, not traced.
' RE-RECORDED UNDER go1.26.10, 2026-11-10 (delivery plan, B12). The full run
' failed the same 15 tests; the flake row passed in that run. The list did
' not change.
'
' Pinned by internal/contract/mise_gates_test.go:
'   TestUnitBaselineRowsNameRealTests       sorted, unique, one test each, and
'                                           the anchored pattern matches each
'                                           name alone
'   TestBaselineSkipsExactlyTheListedTests  the exact run string and usage
'   TestUnitLanesOfferNoRace                -race only behind --no-race

component """go test -race -count=1\n-skip='^(<list>)$' ./...""" as RUN <<app>>
database """[vars] unit_baseline""\nmise.toml · 15 failures · 1 flake" as LIST <<db>>
component "any failure, build error\nor panic · exit 1" as NEW <<error>>
component "the 'passes here' note\nand per-package scope\nLOST 2026-11-12" as FIXED <<error>>
component """mise run ci""\nred on this host at main" as CI <<error>>

LIST ARROW_MAIN RUN : -skip, anchored
RUN ARROW_MAIN NEW : go test's exit code
FIXED ARROW_ERROR LIST : a listed test never runs here
CI ARROW_ERROR RUN : cannot tell old red from new

note bottom of LIST
  **Host-shaped, so it only shrinks by hand.**
  Thirteen rows are macOS tooling failures.
  A row leaves when its test passes on both
  host types, not when one host says so.
end note

note bottom of NEW
  **A build error counts.** go test fails a
  package that does not compile, and -skip
  names tests, never packages, so a slice
  cannot break a package and read green.
end note

note bottom of FIXED
  **A stale row stays silent.** The gate
  skips a listed test instead of running it,
  so only test-go shows a row that passes.
end note

note bottom of CI
  **Why not fix the fifteen first.** None is in
  a TUI package, and thirteen need a Linux
  host to judge. The owner chose to gate on
  "no new failure" instead.
end note
@enduml
